  "proposal": {
    "topic": "pydantic-v2 build/release pattern for ai-factory",
    "paragraph": "ai-factory should adopt a kimi-cli-style single-source-of-truth release pattern built on `uv` + `uv_build` backend pinned to a Pydantic v2 ecosystem. Version is kept static and canonical in each sub-package's `pyproject.toml` `[project] version`, with an automated PR-gate checker (`scripts/check_version_tag.py` analog) asserting cross-package alignment; the build stage injects a provenance build-SHA into a generated `_build_info.py` (via a small `uv run python scripts/inject_build_sha.py` step) so telemetry can distinguish official vs fork/dirty builds, then `uv build --package <pkg> --no-sources --out-dir dist` emits sdist+wheel. Publishing fires only on numeric git tags (`push: tags: [0-9]*`) through `pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish` using OIDC/`__token__`, with per-file SHA256 sums and a generated GitHub Release (softprops/action-gh-release, generate_release_notes) as a secondary artifact; `make check-kimi-cli`-style `check`/`test`/`build`/`build-bin` Makefile targets plus prek hooks keep CI deterministic. For binary/standalone delivery, mirror the `kimi.spec` PyInstaller pattern: a single spec file producing both onefile (default) and onedir (PYINSTALLER_ONEDIR) executables, archived as `{product}-{tag}-{target}.tar.gz/.zip` with sha256 sidecars, and a Nix flake (uv2nix overlay) exposing `nix run .#<product>`. Lint/type is `ruff check`+format + `pyright` (strict on src) + `ty` (non-blocking, `|| true`), all driven by `uv run` so the toolchain is reproducible from `uv.lock`."
  },
